{"file":"Portfolio Interview-1.3.0-v2.zip","bytes":578347,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"portfolio-interview","displayName":"Portfolio Interview","description":"Fully agentic portfolio creation for Claude Code: a state-aware router, eight full skill packs, graph-aligned subagents, deterministic build/QA tooling, hooks, bilingual RTL support, and approval-gated publishing.","version":"1.3.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/imMamdouhaboammar/portfolio-interview","homepage":"https://github.com/imMamdouhaboammar/portfolio-interview","keywords":["portfolio","agentic-workflow","subagents","agent-skills","personal-website","seo","geo","json-ld","arabic","rtl","static-site"]}],"skills":[{"path":"SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-interview","description":"Interview the user through a short guided interview rounds, using popups when the host provides them (field, goals, identity, work, avatar photo, social accounts), then generate a responsive, bilingual-ready personal portfolio website modelled on the imMamdouhaboammar portfolio, fully prepared for SEO and GEO (Person/ProfilePage/FAQPage JSON-LD, hreflang, llms.txt, AI-crawler robots, sitemap, share image). Use when someone asks to build, make or generate a portfolio, personal website, profile page, CV site, \"about me\" page or link-in-bio site, or says \"اعملي بورتفوليو\", \"عايز موقع شخصي\", \"صفحة بروفايل\", \"موقع CV\". Adapts sections, schema types, tone and visual style to the person's field (developer, designer, marketer, writer, creator, photographer, product, consultant, academic, educator, law/medicine/finance).","headings":["Portfolio Interview","Multi-skill architecture","Files","Asking questions","Subagents and hooks","Host portability","Workflow","Publishing","Editing later","Guardrails"],"name_hint":"portfolio · interview"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-audit/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-audit","description":"Use to review an existing generated portfolio for factual provenance, privacy, accessibility, responsive behavior, Arabic RTL, broken links, rendering, SEO/GEO metadata and release regressions. Requires actual artifacts for claims of inspection and returns reproducible severity-tagged findings plus repair routes.","headings":["Portfolio Audit — evidence, accessibility, rendering and SEO QA","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · 审查"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-build/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-build","description":"Use when approved portfolio facts, copy and layout must be generated or regenerated as the repository's static website. Runs the canonical builder and checks when execution exists, records build evidence, protects user work from accidental overwrite, and never claims files, screenshots or checks that were not actually produced.","headings":["Portfolio Build — deterministic static-site generation","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · 构建"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-design/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-design","description":"Use for portfolio information architecture, section hierarchy, responsive visual direction, design tokens, bilingual/RTL behavior, accessibility and UX repair once messaging is approved. Produces a layout decision record for the existing static-site generator and identifies when a real template capability change is required.","headings":["Portfolio Design — information architecture, responsive UX and RTL","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · 设计"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-interview/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-interview","description":"Use when the portfolio workflow needs direct user input that cannot be recovered safely from approved sources: missing facts, target reader, positioning, language/register, visual preferences, confidentiality, public contact choices, or explicit approval gates. Produces a minimal state patch and approval ledger without re-asking known facts.","headings":["Portfolio Interview — targeted elicitation and approvals","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · interview"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-publish/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-publish","description":"Use only when the user explicitly requests publishing or deploying a reviewed portfolio to an approved destination. Requires verified QA plus separate publication and public-contact approvals, protects credentials, records deployment evidence and post-release verification, and stops when host access is unavailable.","headings":["Portfolio Publish — authorization-gated release","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · publish"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-router/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-router","description":"Use as the entry skill for ambiguous, multi-step, repair-heavy or approval-gated portfolio requests. Classifies intent, reads shared state, resolves prerequisites, selects the smallest valid specialist chain, enforces verification/approval boundaries, validates handoffs and reroutes after failures without performing specialist work itself.","headings":["Portfolio Router — state-aware orchestration","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · router"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-source/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-source","description":"Use when portfolio facts must be extracted or verified from a CV, resume, LinkedIn export, GitHub profile, old website, case-study files, testimonials, analytics or other supplied sources. Produces a consent-aware evidence ledger, conflicts and prioritized gaps; use before writing when claims are not already confirmed.","headings":["Portfolio Source — evidence intake and provenance","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · source"},{"path":"skills/portfolio-story/SKILL.md","name":"portfolio-story","description":"Use to write, rewrite or localize approved portfolio headlines, summaries, About sections, project case studies, services and SEO metadata in English or Arabic. Requires confirmed source facts and maps factual copy back to evidence; use when messaging changes, not for layout or unsupported fact creation.","headings":["Portfolio Story — evidence-grounded narrative and localization","Mission","Activate when","Do not use this skill to","Full-pack map","Required inputs","Trust and execution boundary","Step-by-step workflow","Verification gates","Primary output contract","Failure and recovery","Handoffs","Acceptance"],"name_hint":"portfolio · story"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Portfolio Interview","English","What you get","Install","Why this is a mar